	TITLE	MSX-DOS 1 - MSXDOS.SYS 1.03
	SUBTTL	Master file
	.Z80
;******************************************************************************
;
;        Source code of MSXDOS.SYS 1.03, the part of MSX-DOS 1 that is loaded
; from disk at boot time. It provides the CP/M style environment that the
; DOS 1 kernel in the disk ROM lacks: the BDOS entry point at 0005h, the
; partial CP/M BIOS jump table pointed by the jump at 0000h, the disk error
; and Ctrl-C handlers, and the code that loads (or re-enters) COMMAND.COM.
;
;        Reverse engineered from the original MSXDOS.SYS 1.03, copyright (1984)
; Microsoft, starting from the disassembly by Luis C. Grosso (2006). The
; assembled file is identical to the original one, except for the padding
; areas, which are zero filled here.
;
;        This file just puts together the modules, which are:
;
;   head.mac    Entry jump and relocation table.
;   loader.mac  Code that relocates the rest of the file to high memory.
;   sys.mac     The code that runs in high memory.
;
;        The code in loader.mac and sys.mac (the "relocatable part") is
; copied to the top of the TPA and adjusted there for its new address. This
; requires a table with the addresses of all the bytes that hold the high
; byte of an address that points inside the relocatable part. This table is
; generated by assembling the relocatable part twice, at two addresses that
; are one page apart, and comparing the two results: any differing byte is
; the high byte of an address that needs relocating (see the Makefile). For
; this to work, the relocatable part starts on a page boundary, and it
; contains no references to labels in head.mac.
;
;        The table is in reltab.inc, generated by the Makefile when the
; relocatable part is assembled alone (RELBASE defined to its address).
;
;******************************************************************************
;
	include	"../include/dos1.inc"
;
RELTAB	EQU	TPA+3		; The relocation table is right after the
				;   initial jump.
;
	IFDEF	RELBASE
	 ORG	RELBASE		; Relocatable part only.
	ELSE
	 ORG	TPA
	 include "head.mac"
	ENDIF
	include	"loader.mac"
	include	"sys.mac"
;
	END
